1. Claim 15 (Currently amended): A method for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers in a computer network to send data to a client computer, the method comprising the steps of:
accessing a server computer through a path in the computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, wherein the information is added by a media request broker that receives the locator from the client computer;
the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier; and
selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator by the media request broker, __wherein the media request broker selects the first server computer based on load balancing information and server availability metrics not disclosed in the locator itself__.

2. Claim 16 (Currently amended): The method of claim 15, __wherein the second server computer is a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the method further comprising the steps of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, and transmitting the http request to the media request broker which analyzes the unique signature to determine server selection criteria beyond the information contained in the hyperlink itself__.

3. Claim 17 (Currently amended): The method of claim 15, __further comprising the step of the media request broker receiving the information from the client computer and analyzing the information using dynamic load balancing algorithms to select the first server computer__.

4. Claim 18 (Currently amended): The method of claim 17, __wherein the media request broker selects the first server computer based on real-time server performance metrics and network topology information in addition to the information received from the client computer__.

5. Claim 24 (Currently amended): A system for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers in a computer network to send data to a client computer, the system comprising:
a client computer;
a first server computer;
a second server computer;
a path in the computer network connecting the client computer through one or more server computers;
__a media request broker module configured to receive a locator from the client computer and add information indicative of at least one server computer to the locator, wherein the information added by the media request broker includes load balancing data and server availability metrics not present in the original locator__; and
a selection module configured to select the first server computer based on the information added to the locator by the media request broker, __wherein the selection is based on dynamic criteria beyond the static information contained in the locator__.

6. Claim 25 (Currently amended): The system of claim 24, __wherein the second server computer is a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the system further comprising circuitry for selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, and circuitry for transmitting the http request to the media request broker which processes the unique signature to determine server selection criteria independent of the hyperlink content__.

7. Claim 27 (Currently amended): A computer program product for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers in a computer network to send data to a client computer, the computer program product comprising:
a computer-readable medium; and
program instructions stored on the computer-readable medium, the program instructions configured to:
access a server computer through a path in the computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
add information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, __wherein a media request broker module adds the information using dynamic load balancing algorithms and real-time server metrics not disclosed in the locator itself__;
identify the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier; and
select the first server computer based on the information added to the locator by the media request broker, __wherein the selection criteria include server performance data and network conditions analyzed independently of the locator content__.

8. Claim 28 (Currently amended): The computer program product of claim 27, __wherein the second server computer is a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the computer program product further comprising the program step of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, and transmitting the http request to the media request broker which analyzes the unique signature using server selection algorithms that incorporate data beyond the information contained in the hyperlink__.
